The arch-lich alone is a reason to retreat *immediately* and not come
back before you're ready; that means MR and (semi-)permanent engraving
tools. For the black dragon alone you should have reflection. You
probably know that, so just accept that you will not get that bones
loot any time soon. If you're just after the luckstone you can levelport
past the multi-bones level - don't forget to skip that level also on
your way back.

If you have some means to reliably avoid the touch of death and if you
are resistant to disintegration...
With a bit care you can do some tactical maneuvres to let the monsters
come in between the dragon and yourself; occasionally some critters
will just disintegrate without any effort. I do that whenever possible.
If you have MR and are not resistant to disintegration you might solve
the latter problem by carrying a couple of worthless shields; retreat
and put on the next shield until all monsters have been disintegrated.

Hope there's some suggestion that suit you.

